-- title:
--   Norm sweep near a scalar along a fixed torus
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields, $\sigma$ a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$, $v$ a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion and $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, on which $\sigma$ acts through the left factor; for $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ let $N(\delta) = \prod_{i=0}^{n-1} \sigma^i(\delta)$ with $n = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ factors (`normString`, the entrywise $\sigma$-action on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ applied $i$ times), let $T^\sigma_\delta = \{t : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ (`twistedCentralizer`), and call $g$ regular semisimple when $\operatorname{tr}(g)^2 - 4\det(g)$ is a unit. Let $c \in K_v^\times$ and $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ be such that the scalar matrix $c$ is a norm of $\delta$, i.e. $1 \otimes (c \cdot 1) = y^{-1} N(\delta) y$ for some $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$; let $u_0 \in T^\sigma_\delta$, let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ be regular semisimple, and let $y_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ satisfy $1 \otimes \gamma_0 = y_0^{-1} N(u_0\delta) y_0$. The assertion is that for every neighbourhood $V$ of $1$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ there is a neighbourhood $W$ of the scalar matrix $c$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ such that every regular semisimple $\gamma \in W$ lying in the centralizer of $\{\gamma_0\}$ admits $u \in V$ with $u \in T^\sigma_\delta$, $u \in T^\sigma_{u_0\delta}$, $N(u\delta)$ regular semisimple, and $1 \otimes \gamma = y_0^{-1} N(u\delta) y_0$ — the same conjugator $y_0$ for all such $\gamma$.
--
--   This is the local norm-sweep step in the comparison of twisted orbital integrals for base change along $L/K$: regular elements of the torus $T_{\gamma_0} \subset \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ close to the scalar $c$ are norms of twists $u\delta$ of $\delta$ by small elements of the twisted centralizer, realised through a single fixed conjugator. It feeds the elliptic transport and straightening statement [`AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_straighten_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_straighten_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two), and rests on the extraction of $n$-th roots near the identity inside the commutative algebra generated by $\gamma_0$.
